<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Harbor.E2E.Framework.Tests — the unit tests for Harbor.E2E.Framework itself.

    WHY THIS PROJECT EXISTS AT ALL
    ==============================
    TUnit discovers the test classes of a REFERENCED TEST PROJECT inside every
    project that references it. `StateTestRunnerTests` used to live in
    `tests/Harbor.E2E.Framework/`, and six test projects reference that
    framework, so its 26 tests ran six times per CI run: 156 executions of 26
    tests, in six different modules, for one behaviour.

    Moving the file here ends that: nothing references this project, so its
    tests are discovered exactly once, in exactly one module, and they cannot
    be dropped by a TUnit tree-node filter that names some other project's
    classes.

    The rule that keeps this shape is
    `tests/Harbor.Architecture.Tests/TestProjectReferenceRules.cs`:

      * a test project must not reference another test project unless it uses
        its types, and
      * a test project that another test project references must not declare
        test methods at all.

    The second half is the one this project exists to satisfy: the framework
    is referenced by five projects, so it may hold helpers but not tests.

    WHAT IS UNDER TEST NOW (issue #1812)
    ====================================
    The tests that moved here in #1943 asserted on `StateTestRunner`, and
    `StateTestRunner` had no consumer anywhere in the tree: the state-based
    E2E harness it was written for was never wired to a scenario, so the 26
    tests were green and guarded a helper nobody called. `StateTestRunner` is
    gone, and the tests here now cover the helpers the OTHER five E2E
    projects depend on at run time:

      * AnsiStripper       — the scrubber that turns a renderer's raw ANSI
                             bytes into the plain text a test searches for
                             (TuiDriver calls it on every chunk).
      * AnsiTerminalBuffer — the 2D terminal emulator the screen is read out
                             of. Every PTY scenario in
                             Harbor.Tui.CellForge.PtyTests asserts on its
                             rows, and TuiDriver searches the same buffer.

    Both are `internal`, so the framework declares
    `<InternalsVisibleTo Include="Harbor.E2E.Framework.Tests"/>`.

    The tests are pure: no PTY, no display server, no mock LLM server. That
    is why they are a separate project rather than one more class in an E2E
    suite.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>false</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>false</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1591;CA1707;CA1861;S5445;S3011</NoWarn>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- The subject under test. Declared explicitly, not leaned on transitively. -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Harbor.E2E.Framework\Harbor.E2E.Framework.csproj"/>
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
